WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.240
Why have you invited us here?!
- I didn’t. I told him not to prod.

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.160
She wanted to conceal it from you.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.800
Calm down, calm down.
Please be quiet!

4
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.080
We’re having a family council.
We have to decide what to do about this.

5
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.360
A divorce is not a joke!

6
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.440
DIVORCE IN PEACE

7
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.080
Right. Very good.
Let’s talk about it.

8
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.320
You think you have
absolutely nothing in common?

9
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.160
Well, yes… On mental level.

10
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.480
Again a very exaggerated
and biased statement.

11
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.560
The simplest things –
I have yoga classes,

12
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.720
you are sitting at your computer.
In your conservative club?

13
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.520
That’s the same thing –
worry about cosmic balance.

14
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.120
The only difference is

15
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.720
that you selfishly worry
about your personal balance,

16
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.960
I’m worried for the whole world.

17
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.200
Let’s be honest,
the whole thing is slanted, very slanted!

18
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.240
There you can vent your anger.

19
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.840
Instead of changing yourself,
which would be something real.

20
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.800
What are you talking about!
How have you come to this point?

21
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.160
Because it’s important, right?

22
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.800
I don’t know. We do have common…

23
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.240
We had common… hobbies.

24
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:34.440
Music… favourite songs.

25
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.960
You listen to your music so loud
and we’re sitting, headphones on,

26
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.280
just to have some kind of life.
Favourite songs! Really!

27
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.560
What the point in this whacking
here, like this?

28
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.320
It’s total masochism.
Who needs this?

29
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.120
No, no. That’s very good.

30
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:55.880
That’s why we are here -
to whack in safe environment.

31
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.200
OK. Excuse me, it’s my opinion.
Sorry, I’m really sorry.

32
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.360
What was the next mission?

33
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.760
Right, next one is...

34
00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.680
“Thanksgiving dinner”.

35
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.200
You’ll organise a nice dinner
to thank each other for the past.

36
00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.240
I would like you to change routine.

37
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.840
Husband would cook,
wife would make a fire.

38
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.200
I have usually done both
and then washed the dishes.

39
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.040
Then I have trimmed the hedge,

40
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.560
because Aksel simply can’t stand
any kind of asymmetry.

41
00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.160
Stop it! What are you talking about?
I have done all kind of housework.

42
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.360
You come home late at night
and fall into the world of invoices.

43
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.000
There! Another thing
we completely agree on.

44
00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:50.920
Can’t understand. If there was
adultery or quarrel or something.

45
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.640
I simply can’t understand.
- I can’t either.

46
00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.720
Laura wants to get a divorce.
Maybe out of boredom?

47
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.080
What marriage means to you?

48
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.160
Even in animal kingdom all is clear.
Take a stork. Take a penguin.

49
00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.920
Take a kangaroo. Take a swan.
All is clear for them.

50
00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:23.760
But for our daughter nothing is clear.
- Maybe I’m not enough swan for her.

51
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:31.480
You are! You are all right.
Remember, you’ll always be our son.

52
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.880
Right? Even if…

53
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:42.680
Look now! Educated, talented,
kind, sensitive man… and Laura?

54
00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.760
What will she do with her life
at her age?

55
00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.560
Would she ever find somebody…
Oh my god!

56
00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:58.960
Damn, damn! Kind of fashion statement.
Let’s all get a divorce!

57
00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.720
Soon we’ll smoke grass
and live happily ever after.

58
00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:09.280
I also thought it was a kind of whim,
but now I’ll see that…

59
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.640
I’ll go and speak with her.

60
00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.880
I can’t stand up.

61
00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.280
Thank you.

62
00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.320
Alright.

63
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.880
Let’s come clean!
What’s the matter?

64
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.600
I tell you, I don’t…
I don’t know what’s matter with her.

65
00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.800
I can’t understand.

66
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.200
Don’t be shy.

67
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:55.520
It… It may be…

68
00:04:55.640 --> 00:05:00.400
Well, simply an intimate matter.

69
00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:06.440
I have no intimate problems…
All’s well. Nothing has been found.

70
00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.880
Don’t be shy. No need.
These things happen. To all men.

71
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.600
When there are problems.
- What problems?

72
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.480
What I want to say…

73
00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.800
There are all kind of miracle doctors,

74
00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:29.000
pills, food additives
plus mechanical gadgets.

75
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:34.320
When women want, one has to go along.

76
00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.280
Well, once a year.

77
00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:45.600
There’s nothing wrong with me.
All is well in this sense... with that.

78
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.960
Mine is functioning.

79
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.680
Functioning?

80
00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:01.640
Pardon me! Pardon me!
I can’t understand a thing!

81
00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.240
Please go home
before it’s getting dark.

82
00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:11.360
We’ll speak later,
during a weekend.

83
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:18.160
Promise you’ll do nothing thoughtless
we all will regret.

84
00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.960
Children, broken family.
Dear god!

85
00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.280
Remember, we are Estonians.

86
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:29.040
When we marry, that’s for life.

87
00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.960
Sweat drops in the forehead, grinding...

88
00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:40.640
But living together.
- Yes, grinding.

89
00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.320
What? It’s my mother calling!

90
00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:48.720
Oh yes. I called your mother
and I called Julia and Rein too.

91
00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.480
Ciao!
- Hello.

92
00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.600
Thank you.

93
00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:17.160
So, all is well?
- Yes.

94
00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.640
Not really.
I will get a divorce.

95
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.680
Yesterday was a totally crazy day.
My parents fell on us. Madhouse!

96
00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.200
Poor thing!

97
00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:46.840
Oh well, life goes on and...
No problems.

98
00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:53.320
What about this cake shop?
- What about it?

99
00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.560
Now when you are getting a divorce...?

100
00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.880
Hell! He will not get the shop.
I built it, it’s my life’s achievement.

101
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.160
All will remain as it is.

102
00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:14.400
Let’s be all really polite and kind
to mommy and no sulking, all right?

103
00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.320
Dad, have you noticed,
we’re not five years old anymore?

104
00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.920
Yes, right… You are…

105
00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.720
I’ll graduate from university,
I have a partner.

106
00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.440
You have a partner?

107
00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.840
Dear god...! Yes, I told you. Ülo.

108
00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.800
He will come here tomorrow.

109
00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:38.320
OK, very nice. Timing is not perfect
at the moment, but that’s good.

110
00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:43.400
Your own guy is very good.
Specially now.., when we… yes…

111
00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:48.800
Anyway, I want us to cooperate,
together we might convince mother.

112
00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.800
Yes, I…

113
00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.600
I want us to stay together
for our own sake.

114
00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.960
No, you are concerned for yourself.

115
00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.520
Mom has nothing to worry about,
when she gets a divorce.

116
00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:05.720
She is earning real money, while you are…
- What about me?

117
00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.560
You are a violin teacher.

118
00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:13.960
It’s a very respectable profession.
Money doesn’t bring happiness.

119
00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.560
You are too lazy, simply lazy.

120
00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:17.960
You can’t understand,

121
00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:22.320
you have to organise all by yourself
and to rent and who knows what. - Ave!

122
00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:27.480
Ave! Don’t Ave me.
Dear god, why I’m talking to you.

123
00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.320
You can’t even understand,
how immoral and cruel is to eat meat!

124
00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:36.480
In that case I could stop eating meat.

125
00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.800
I quit smoking, meat’s not a problem.

126
00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.720
I’ll start slowly from shoulder till
I’ve no desire even for chicken wings.

127
00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:47.880
Aksel, what do you want from us?

128
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.240
I want us to create a very cosy,
warm atmosphere here, at home.

129
00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.400
For mother to have good time.
I have a plan.

130
00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:02.200
With Tauno we thought I’ll find a hobby
to share with your mother

131
00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.080
so we could go on with life together.

132
00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.240
Go on where?

133
00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:15.480
Listen, children.
Life isn’t that bad.

134
00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.240
It’s worth saving.

135
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:53.160
Of course, Tauno is on Aksel’s side,
but I understand you very well.

136
00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.560
Thank you.

137
00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:59.960
I feel pity too. It’s your energy,
life’s energy and it must be cared for.

138
00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.440
Thanks.

139
00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.080
Take a breath.

140
00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:11.560
Deep breath.
Lay back, flat on your back.

141
00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:20.560
Now breathe calmly in and out.

142
00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:28.880
This I will say you can’t get a divorce
before you have tried all options.

143
00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.640
What?

144
00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.840
I just couldn’t say no to him.

145
00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.360
What?

146
00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.440
What are you doing here?

147
00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:41.840
Common hobbies, darling.
Time spent together.

148
00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:45.640
Mirjam?
- Aksel told you had no common hobbies.

149
00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.320
Jesus, really!
You too, Miriam.

150
00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.200
Not me too. Tauno told me.
Tauno insisted.

151
00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.720
Let me try at least.

152
00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:55.120
I don’t know.
This is a total invasion right now.

153
00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:58.600
Come here and sit quietly down.
You’ll follow all the exercises, right?

154
00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:02.840
Still as a mouse.
I’ll sit like mouse, a mute mouse.

155
00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:06.280
Aksel, it doesn‘t work like this,
upon command. You know that.

156
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.920
It’s something… a kind of step…

157
00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.600
Right.
- It’s a kind of step.

158
00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:15.960
You were to organise this thanksgiving
dinner. - It’ll be… it’ll be impressive.

159
00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.720
Asked parents to help you out?
- Laura, please.

160
00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.400
I don’t know, my blood pressure
is going up already right now.

161
00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:30.160
Lay back. Right.
Now breathe in and out.

162
00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.000
And the hands.

163
00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.160
Calmly in and out.

164
00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.800
Out with your voice.

165
00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.760
You too, Aksel.

166
00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:56.440
Laura, this thanksgiving dinner...
I will start organising.

167
00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.560
I have to go shopping...
I have a list...

168
00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.560
That’s nice.

169
00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:04.280
I’ll organise everything myself,
you have nothing to worry about.

170
00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.440
And?

171
00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:10.920
Right, only... I have to go shopping.
I mean...

172
00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.880
Well?

173
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.840
I have to go shopping, I mean...

174
00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.600
I will be paid day after tomorrow.

175
00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:31.480
A couple of students dropped out,
but that’s normal in high culture.

176
00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:35.720
This kind of fluc... fluctuation.

177
00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:41.280
Music School will pay my salary.
- OK. Don’t worry.

178
00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:47.440
No. It’s your money earned from bakery,
I don’t need it.

179
00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.920
I’ll manage myself perfectly.

180
00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:59.360
I’ll show you.
All will change for the better.

181
00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:02.720
Mother, father. Ülo is here.
- Ülo who?

182
00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:05.920
My guy.
- How have you forgotten, Aksel?

183
00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:10.280
Right, yes... Should come today.
Of course, your guy.

184
00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:14.600
Very nice. We can combine this
with our thanksgiving dinner.

185
00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:15.680
But...

186
00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:17.640
Ülo, come in.

187
00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.880
Hello.

188
00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.720
Honestly.

189
00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:43.520
He is ten years older than me.
At least ten years.

190
00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.680
Sugar daddy?

191
00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:52.600
No. Ave’s former university lecturer.
Art teacher. A kind of failed sculptor.

192
00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:59.880
Those fucking excrement artists!
Is this even legal?

193
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.840
Ave is 23, legally she can move in
with Tutankhamun’s mummy.

194
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.360
If she want to.

195
00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.680
Well, it’s a little surprising
to put it mildly.

196
00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:16.960
It’s... honestly, it’s not serious?

197
00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.720
Obviously our daughter
has been missing a father figure.

198
00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:24.400
I see. Thank you, mother figure!

199
00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:27.720
Now we’ll wait till Mihkel comes home
with your classmate. Then it’s full set.

200
00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:31.400
Calm down. If Ave had made this choice,
we have to respect this.

201
00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.840
So, please...

202
00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.520
I understand father is cooking
a dinner in Ülo’s honour?

203
00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:43.320
This dinner was intended
to be more general...

204
00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.040
Ülo can help you.

205
00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:48.360
No, no, I’ll manage. Thanks!
Now I have to go shopping.

206
00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:53.240
Ülo can help you there too.
- No need. I’ll manage, will go.

207
00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:01.480
Honestly, Ave is protesting
against this situation between us.

208
00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.000
She can’t seriously like this man?

209
00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:09.440
Women sometimes don’t know,
what they really want.

210
00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:12.960
All is falling apart. Bloody hell!

211
00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:19.880
Brother, don’t bleed!
Cook a proper dinner for your wife.

212
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.280
Then you’ll take her to the theatre.
Tickets are here.

213
00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:27.960
Here is deer’s liver.

214
00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:34.440
And here is recipe.

215
00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:38.280
You’ll follow recipe precisely
and she wouldn’t get a divorce.

216
00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.120
And eat the recipe!

217
00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:45.720
Nobody eats meat in our house.
Nobody. I promised to quit too.

218
00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:49.360
It’s polluting oceans
or something...

219
00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:53.080
Don’t bullshit!
Just follow the recipe.

220
00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:57.560
These silo eaters will ask for more.
Will cry and ask for more.

221
00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:59.600
I’ll go and empty my bladder.

222
00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.840
Ave? Mihkel?

223
00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.480
Tõnu?
– Mart.

224
00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:35.440
Hello, Aksel.
We have to talk.

225
00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:36.960
About what?

226
00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.080
What’s wrong... ?
- Onion.

227
00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.840
Right. The thing is
that Elle told me everything.

228
00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.360
What everything?

229
00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:49.400
Everything that happened
at Music School’s Christmas party.

230
00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.640
What... Good heavens!
Nothing happened.

231
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:55.000
Do you want to explain it in front
of your neighbours or invite me in?

232
00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.080
Mart, I have nothing to explain.

233
00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:00.840
You harassed and stalked my wife
and now there’s nothing to explain?

234
00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.200
I have not harassed your wife.

235
00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:07.440
We were dancing. Consensual.
It was just a dance as at any party.

236
00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.120
Nothing happened.
Elle herself said that nothing happened.

237
00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.920
From what I hear things happened.
Quite a lot happened.

238
00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:17.120
Nothing happened, Mart.
Please, I can’t explain right now.

239
00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.040
Believe me, all is well.
Nothing happened.

240
00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.760
I want you to stop harassing my wife!
- I don’t harass her.

241
00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.800
And stalking and you have to apologise.
Elle is totally freaking out.

242
00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.280
What’d you mean freaking out?
What did I do? Nothing has happened!

243
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.120
How come? Why did you stalk her?

244
00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:33.800
I saw you with Elle through the window.
That’s why began to...

245
00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.440
Hello. What is going on?
- Nothing is going on. This is Laura.

246
00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:41.160
Yes it is! I can explain right away.
The thing is...

247
00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.960
There’s nothing to explain.
Leave right away, Mart!

248
00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:47.800
I demand you’ll stop harassing.
I can call the police.

249
00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.720
Police? Why police?

250
00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:53.800
These people have gone crazy.
It’s all lies. Hit the road! Don’t interfere.

251
00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:56.360
If you have courage to harass,
have courage to admit it too.

252
00:18:56.480 --> 00:19:00.840
Who did you harass? Elle?
- Exactly. Elle is totally freaked out.

253
00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:06.160
Elle is not freaked out.
She liked... what I actually didn’t do.

254
00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:11.920
I haven’t harassed her
and nothing happened. Exactly!

255
00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:16.320
Everything that didn’t happen
was nicely consensual and great.

256
00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.920
Can’t understand a thing.

257
00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.120
Harasser!
- You are slanderer!

258
00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:24.840
Harasser!
Don’t touch me! Are you crazy?

259
00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:27.560
The deer!

260
00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:36.040
Ouch! Shit!
Bloody hell!

261
00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:49.480
So funny! I wanted to get a divorce
before this mess and now...

262
00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:53.040
now I want it even more.

263
00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:56.240
It’s absurd. Completely absurd!

264
00:19:56.360 --> 00:20:00.280
Yes, I danced with Elle at the party.
This is true.

265
00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:04.720
Then Elle suddenly cornered me
behind a freezer and imposed upon me.

266
00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.560
With force, you know.

267
00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.400
I withdraw as if hit by lightning,
but she was imposing on.

268
00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:15.160
You can’t believe how I resisted.
I resisted really really hard.

269
00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:23.200
Then you stalked her really hard?
- No, no. I just happened to be there.

270
00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:30.080
When I saw her, I tried to avoid her,
but she clung to me, didn’t let go.

271
00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:35.200
She must have feelings for me.
I think.

272
00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.360
I noticed that, now I get it.

273
00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:43.160
Back then, when I went to
this music school to earn extra money.

274
00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:48.040
Extra money? That’s your only salary.
With private lessons you earn nothing.

275
00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:52.240
Well... extra money can be more
and more stable than main income.

276
00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:55.680
What’s the difference!
- You’re right. There’s no difference.

277
00:20:55.800 --> 00:21:01.080
Laura, this is...
This mess has really bad timing.

278
00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:04.000
This changes nothing.
I’ll hire a lawyer.

279
00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.280
What?

280
00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:08.560
He’ll make sure our joint property
will be divided fairly.

281
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.000
What?

282
00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:18.080
I don’t want us to turn into monsters,
when diving the property.

283
00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.840
In these cases
intermediator is recommended.

284
00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:26.160
That’s really sick! Some article crook
will start organising our life.

285
00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:29.440
A legal notch will audit our life!

286
00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:34.560
Are we some sociopathic newly-rich,
who can’t manage the property normally?

287
00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:38.000
But we can’t. You already have
bandages on your hand.

288
00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:40.360
I don’t want things to escalate.

289
00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.640
You’ll invite a specialist,
who will draw the lines.

290
00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:47.480
My god! Well, Laura…

291
00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.000
Thanks!

292
00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:55.240
This was a nice thanksgiving dinner.
- I didn’t have a chance.

293
00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.000
25 years have been a very long time
for a chance.

294
00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:03.760
Shit!

295
00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.880
Ciao, Mona.

296
00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:11.280
Listen, I have some good news.

297
00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:15.280
I’ll think I know what to do
for term paper. Finally.

298
00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:17.360
Well, I told you shouldn’t worry.

299
00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:21.840
I’ll shoot a reality show
about my parent’s divorce.

300
00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:23.520
Directly from the source,

301
00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:27.680
my own YouTube channel –
“Aksel versus Laura”.

302
00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:31.320
This should prove my talent
to the commission.

303
00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:34.400
Sick! Really cool!

304
00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:38.440
Honestly this was a misunderstanding.
I have nothing to do with this woman,

305
00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:40.440
but try to explain to Laura

306
00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:44.280
that these bloody flute suckers
have gone crazy.

307
00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:48.120
Hell, they have blown their brains out
through the flute

308
00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:51.520
and come to my courtyard
to accuse me, teach me.

309
00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:55.360
Shit, this has really bad timing,
really bad.

310
00:22:55.480 --> 00:23:01.760
True. All is over now.
All has been tried and all is over.

311
00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:03.200
Are you sure?

312
00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:08.720
Of course! There will be a divorce,
everybody for himself.

313
00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:11.440
Laura for herself and I for myself.

314
00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:15.320
Everything cut into half.

315
00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:24.680
Stop these thoughts.
These worries will kill you!

316
00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:28.520
Let the situation to calm down
before you say something like that.

317
00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:30.440
Come, let’s shoot a little.

318
00:23:30.560 --> 00:23:36.040
There’s nothing to calm down.
There’s nothing to do.

319
00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:41.760
There will be ugly and angry divorce.
Now I’ll have to fight for myself.

320
00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:45.480
Honestly, my heart is bleeding.

321
00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:49.080
Good men are not appreciated
in this country.

322
00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:55.440
Aksel, you have to sort this out.
- Mirjam, I was trying to.

323
00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:57.920
You did it all wrong.

324
00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:02.000
Your fussing is not working,
when you’re missing the main point.

325
00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.960
What main point?

326
00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:11.680
Be more intimate.
You know, soft light, a little wine.

327
00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:19.920
Well, at current state…
wouldn’t this be a little phony?

328
00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:24.600
It should be. Do you think
honesty is base for the solid marriage?

329
00:24:24.720 --> 00:24:28.080
Some faking, little fantasy.

330
00:24:29.640 --> 00:24:32.120
Fantasy? What fantasy?

331
00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:35.040
Do I have to spell out everything?

332
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:41.400
Play her violin, in the morning
bring toast and coffee to bed...

333
00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:47.600
Brush your hair, wear nice underwear.
Like a Fiddler on the Roof.

334
00:24:52.840 --> 00:24:55.440
This would work for sure!

335
00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:59.440
Well, I will play violin at home...

336
00:24:59.560 --> 00:25:02.400
Yes, this will work for sure!

337
00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:10.560
What did you mean by faking?

338
00:25:14.080 --> 00:25:18.600
Do you want me to give you a massage?

339
00:25:20.920 --> 00:25:24.160
Little booty massage?

340
00:25:38.840 --> 00:25:42.400
That’s enough, Roberta.

341
00:25:46.960 --> 00:25:50.680
Roberta, have you given a thought,
why are you doing this?

342
00:25:52.160 --> 00:25:56.160
Why do you have to learn
to play violin?

343
00:25:57.280 --> 00:26:02.480
Let’s all play violin!
Why you really need this skill?

344
00:26:03.760 --> 00:26:07.120
I don’t know…
- Because your mother wants this?

345
00:26:07.240 --> 00:26:09.800
Because your father,
uncles, aunts want?

346
00:26:09.920 --> 00:26:13.680
So nice, we have a daughter,
who can play violin!

347
00:26:13.800 --> 00:26:17.440
I dreamt of big stages.

348
00:26:17.560 --> 00:26:20.640
Practiced all the time,
had no time to sleep.

349
00:26:20.760 --> 00:26:25.320
When I finally got on this stage,
I wet my pants out of fear.

350
00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:30.560
Turned out all this was not for me.
I was engaged in the wrong thing.

351
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:37.160
I’m walking around without knowing
what I really want. Like in a blur.

352
00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:39.840
Ouch!
– Sorry!

353
00:26:46.480 --> 00:26:51.640
On Wednesday we’ll have a longer lesson.
Very good. - This is yours.

354
00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:57.200
Right, this is mine.

355
00:27:37.240 --> 00:27:39.080
What the hell?

356
00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:45.320
What are you doing here?
- Where is mother?

357
00:27:45.440 --> 00:27:49.880
Went to work already.
She gave her room to Ülo. - What?

358
00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:54.480
Ülo has no place to go. His wife
kicked him out because of me.

359
00:27:54.600 --> 00:27:58.760
They are getting a divorce, you know.
- Really? And mother?

360
00:27:58.880 --> 00:28:03.440
Mother is sleeping in my room.
My bed is too narrow for Ülo.

361
00:28:03.560 --> 00:28:05.920
Really?

362
00:28:06.840 --> 00:28:09.480
You said that everything should be
divided into halves.

363
00:28:09.600 --> 00:28:12.000
Everything should be listed
and the list passed on to the lawyer.

364
00:28:12.120 --> 00:28:17.520
OK. Let’s draw a broader line.
- Broader?

365
00:28:17.640 --> 00:28:21.240
Yes, the bakery.
- You don’t touch it!

366
00:28:21.360 --> 00:28:23.760
Yes I will.
It’s joint property.

367
00:28:23.880 --> 00:28:28.360
My cake shop is not joint property!
I built this business on my own.

368
00:28:28.480 --> 00:28:31.280
I don’t mess with your violin lessons
or your private students.

369
00:28:31.400 --> 00:28:34.240
You can have half of my violin students
if you want to.

370
00:28:34.360 --> 00:28:38.520
I’ll take half of the bakery!
- You want your war? Right?

371
00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:42.360
Velvet gloves are off now.
All is fair in love and war!
